- Reuters reported that the anti-graft drive had begun to damage routine administration and investment flows by late 2022.
  SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Analysis: Vietnam’s anti-graft crackdown chills supply chains, investment","publisher":"ThePrint (Reuters)","publication_date":"2022-11-28","url":"https://theprint.in/world/analysis-vietnams-anti-graft-crackdown-chills-supply-chains-investment/1239091/","claim":"Reuters reported that Vietnam's anti-corruption drive had paralysed many routine transactions, caused shortages of essential goods, and dampened investor confidence, disrupting drug and petrol imports and delaying energy and manufacturing projects.","locator":"lead paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting with specific causal claims, named interviewees, and concrete supply-chain examples.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Strong but mediated. The drive is Trọng-led, but the immediate mechanism runs through bureaucratic caution and official enforcement behavior.","contrary_evidence":["The campaign aimed to discipline corruption and was not solely the cause of every shortage or delay; global price shocks and post-COVID disruption also mattered."],"lenses":["8B.6","8B.8","8B.9","8B.10"]}
